WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.088
Nine rules turn the
intervals into a work list.

2
00:00:03.088 --> 00:00:06.301
S T 1 flags a block slower
than the threshold,

3
00:00:06.301 --> 00:00:11.300
which is P S 4's organization-defined
period; the sample is four hours.

4
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:14.400
S T 2 flags a leaver
who was never blocked.

5
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:18.506
S T 3 flags a separation entered
more than three days late:

6
00:00:18.506 --> 00:00:22.962
a finding if nothing caught it, a
warning if an on-demand run did.

7
00:00:22.962 --> 00:00:26.722
S T 4 flags an uncollected
card revoked more

8
00:00:26.722 --> 00:00:30.900
than eighteen hours after
notice, from FIPS 201-3.

9
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:34.680
And S T 5 flags a re-enable
that HR didn't cancel.
